    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0238" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/516: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-11T00:00:00-04:00">March 11,
                            1942—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1034. Your no. 1050, March 5, 7 p.m. You should inform Sir Alexander Cadogan that
                    we have every desire to assist in the selection <pb facs="0239" n="227"
                        xml:id="pg227"/> of a financial adviser for Iran. The concluding sentence of
                    section 2 of your telegram under reference reflects accurately the Department’s
                    view of the matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
